From 93f33a12519df09951d2db0c71c9eb453138eaaf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rocky59487 <hankqaq.tmd.tw@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 11:30:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(stress): moment-extremum stations, neutral axis,
 clamped-edge shell recovery

Three post-processing capabilities that consumers (the Block Reality sidecar) were
computing by hand outside the engine. Owning them here puts every mechanics number
behind the engine's own gates and leaves adapters with nothing to compute:

- computeStressField(.., includeMomentExtrema): additionally samples each member at
  the analytic interior extremum of its moment diagrams (dM/dx = 0). A uniform grid
  misses a propped cantilever's span peak at x = 5L/8; the screen must not. Default
  off; layout bit-identical when off. Gate: F74 (9wL^2/128 closed form, rel 0).

- MemberStressSample.naY/naZ (+hasNaY/hasNaZ): neutral-axis offset where the linear
  sigma profile crosses zero, y0 = -(N/A)*Iz/Mz, reported only when strictly inside
  the section. Gate: F75 (closed form + definitional sigma(y0) == 0 interlock).

- recoverShellEdgeMoments(model, sr): clamped-edge support-moment recovery
  M_edge ~= 1.5*M1 - 0.5*M2 with the adoption rule 'only ever raises the screened
  demand'. Against Timoshenko's clamped square plate at 8 elements per side the raw
  corner moment is 39.7% low; recovered is 14.0% low. Gate: F76.

frametest: ALL PASS (F1..F76).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
